# Own-words summaries of non-SRD spells (S–Z, and PHB spells missing from the SRD).
NOTES = {
"Sapping Sting": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V, S", "Instantaneous",
  "You sap the vitality of a creature you can see. It makes a Constitution save or takes 1d4 necrotic damage and falls prone. Damage grows to 2d4 at 5th level, 3d4 at 11th and 4d4 at 17th.", ""),
"Scatter": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V", "Instantaneous",
  "The air quivers around up to five creatures of your choice that you can see. An unwilling one makes a Wisdom save to resist. Each affected creature teleports to an unoccupied space you choose within 120 feet of you, on the ground or on a floor.", ""),
"Shadow Blade": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You weave a sword of solid shadow in your hand. It's a simple melee weapon you're proficient with: 2d8 psychic damage, finesse, light and thrown (20/60). If you attack with it from dim light or darkness you have advantage. Drop or throw it and it vanishes, but you can call it back to your hand as a bonus action.", "Damage becomes 3d8 at 3rd or 4th level, 4d8 at 5th or 6th, and 5d8 at 7th or higher."),
"Shadow of Moil": ("1 action", "Self", "V, S, M (an undead eyeball encased in a gem worth 150 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "Flame-like shadows wreathe you. You're heavily obscured to others, you resist radiant damage, and any creature within 10 feet that hits you takes 2d8 necrotic damage.", ""),
"Shape Water": ("1 action", "30 feet", "S", "Instantaneous or 1 hour",
  "You control water in a 5-foot cube: move it or change its flow, shape it into simple forms that move as you wish for an hour, change its color or opacity for an hour, or freeze it (if there are no creatures in it) for an hour.", ""),
"Sickening Radiance": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "Dim, greenish light fills a 30-foot-radius sphere. A creature in it at the start of its turn makes a Constitution save, taking 4d10 radiant damage and a level of exhaustion on a failure, and glows (no hiding, no invisibility). Exhaustion from this spell fades when the spell ends.", ""),
"Silvery Barbs": ("1 reaction, when a creature you can see succeeds on an attack, check or save", "60 feet", "V", "Instantaneous",
  "You throw silvery words that unsettle the creature: it rerolls the d20 and must use the lower roll. Then a different creature of your choice within 60 feet has advantage on its next attack, check or save in the next minute.", ""),
"Skill Empowerment": ("1 action", "Touch", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You touch a willing creature and choose a skill it's proficient in: it gets expertise (double proficiency) in that skill for the duration.", ""),
"Skywrite": ("1 action (ritual)", "Sight", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You write up to ten words in clouds anywhere in the sky you can see. A strong wind can blow them away early.", ""),
"Snare": ("1 minute", "Touch", "S, M (25 feet of rope, consumed)", "8 hours",
  "You set a magical trap on a 5-foot circle on the ground. It's nearly invisible (Intelligence (Investigation) against your DC to spot). A Small or larger creature that steps in makes a Dexterity save or is restrained and hoisted upside down 3 feet in the air. It can try again on each of its turns, or others can free it.", ""),
"Snowball Swarm": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (a piece of ice or small white rock)", "Instantaneous",
  "A flurry of snowballs bursts at a point you choose. Each creature in a 5-foot-radius sphere makes a Dexterity save, taking 3d6 cold damage on a failure or half on a success.", "Damage rises by 1d6 for each level above 2nd."),
"Soul Cage": ("1 reaction, when a humanoid you can see within 60 feet dies", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a tiny silver cage worth 100 gp)", "8 hours",
  "You snatch the soul of a creature as it dies and trap it in the cage. Until the spell ends you can use it, each use once: steal its life (heal 2d8), query it (one question, honest-ish answer), borrow its experience (advantage on one roll), or eyes of the dead (scry a place it saw in life). The soul is freed when the spell ends. (In Avarenth, gods notice such things.)", ""),
"Spellfire Flare": None,
"Spellfire Storm": None,
"Spirit Lantern": None,
"Spirit of Death": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a gilded playing card worth 400 gp depicting an avatar of death)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call up a reaper spirit that obeys you. It hovers, fights on your turn, and its scythe deals necrotic damage that gets stronger with the spell's level. When it reduces a creature to 0 hit points, that creature can't be healed or brought back until the spell ends.", "The spirit grows stronger (more hit points and damage) for each level above 4th."),
"Spirit Shroud": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "Spirits of the dead flit around you. When you hit a creature within 10 feet, it takes an extra 1d8 radiant, necrotic or cold damage (your choice), and it can't regain hit points until the start of your next turn. You can also slow one creature within 10 feet by 10 feet each turn.", "Extra damage rises by 1d8 for every two levels above 3rd."),
"Spray of Cards": ("1 action", "Self (15-foot cone)", "V, S, M (a deck of cards)", "Instantaneous",
  "Razor-sharp spectral cards spray out in a 15-foot cone. Each creature there makes a Dexterity save, taking 2d10 force damage and being blinded until the end of its next turn on a failure, or half damage only on a success.", "Damage rises by 1d10 for each level above 2nd."),
"Staggering Smite": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "Your next melee weapon hit before the spell ends rattles the target's mind: an extra 4d6 psychic damage, and it makes a Wisdom save or has disadvantage on attacks and checks and can't take reactions until the end of its next turn.", ""),
"Steel Wind Strike": ("1 action", "30 feet", "S, M (a melee weapon worth at least 1 sp)", "Instantaneous",
  "You flourish your weapon and vanish, striking at up to five creatures you can see within range. Make a melee spell attack against each: 6d10 force damage on a hit. Then you can teleport to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of one of them.", ""),
"Storm Sphere": ("1 action", "150 feet", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A 20-foot-radius sphere of whirling air forms. It's difficult terrain, and a creature ending its turn there makes a Strength save or takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage. As a bonus action on later turns, you can make a lightning bolt leap from the sphere's center at a creature within 60 feet: a ranged spell attack for 4d6 lightning (with advantage if the target is inside).", "Both damages rise by 1d6 for each level above 4th."),
"Summon Aberration": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (a pickled tentacle and an eyeball in a platinum-inlaid vial worth 400 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call an aberrant spirit: beholderkin (flying, eye ray), slaad (claws, regeneration) or star spawn (psychic slam, whispering aura). It obeys you, acts on your turn, and its numbers (AC, hit points, attacks) scale with the spell's level.", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 4th: more hit points, better AC and damage."),
"Summon Beast": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (a feather, tuft of fur and fish tail inside a gilded acorn worth 200 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call a bestial spirit: air (flies, flyby), land (climbs, pack tactics) or water (swims, breathes water). It obeys you, acts on your turn, and its numbers scale with the spell's level.", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 2nd."),
"Summon Celestial": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (a golden reliquary worth 500 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call a celestial spirit: an avenger (a ranged radiant bow) or a defender (a radiant mace and protective shield). It can also heal once. It obeys you, acts on your turn, and its numbers scale with the spell's level.", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 5th."),
"Summon Construct": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (an ornate stone and metal lockbox worth 400 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call the spirit of a construct: clay (absorbs damage), metal (heated body burns attackers) or stone (slows nearby foes). It obeys you, acts on your turn, and its numbers scale with the spell's level.", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 4th."),
"Summon Dinosaur": None,
"Summon Draconic Spirit": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (an object with the image of a dragon engraved on it, worth 500 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call a draconic spirit (chromatic, gem or metallic). It flies, bites, breathes a cone of its element, and you share its resistance while you're within 10 feet of it. It obeys you, acts on your turn, and its numbers scale with the spell's level.", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 5th."),
"Summon Elemental": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (air, a pebble, ash and water inside a gold-inlaid vial worth 400 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call an elemental spirit: air (flies), earth (burrows), fire (ignites what it hits) or water (grapples). It obeys you, acts on your turn, and its numbers scale with the spell's level.", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 4th."),
"Summon Fey": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (a gilded flower worth 300 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call a fey spirit in a mood: fuming (advantage on its next attack), mirthful (charms) or tricksy (darkness). It teleports a short distance each turn, obeys you, and its numbers scale with the spell's level.", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 3rd."),
"Summon Fiend": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (humanoid blood inside a ruby vial worth 600 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call a fiendish spirit: demon (bites, explodes in fire when slain), devil (hurls flame) or yugoloth (claws and teleport). It obeys you, acts on your turn, and its numbers scale with the spell's level. (In Avarenth, this is demon-touched magic; expect consequences.)", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 6th."),
"Summon Greater Demon": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a vial of blood from a humanoid killed in the past 24 hours)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call a demon of challenge rating 5 or lower. It rolls initiative and acts on its own turn, attacking the nearest non-demon. Each turn you command it, it makes a Charisma save; on a success it breaks free and does as it likes. Draw a blood circle first and it can't leave. (In Avarenth: very much demon business.)", "The demon's challenge rating rises by 1 for each level above 4th."),
"Summon Lesser Demons": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a vial of blood from a humanoid killed in the past 24 hours)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "Roll on a table to call a group of minor demons (several manes, dretches or similar). They're hostile to everyone, attacking the nearest non-demon each turn, though a blood circle keeps them in. (In Avarenth: demon business.)", "More demons appear at 6th and 8th level."),
"Summon Plant": None,
"Summon Shadowspawn": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (tears inside a crystal vial worth 300 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call a shadowy spirit: fury (advantage when frightening), despair (slows nearby foes) or fear (frightens and hides in dim light). It obeys you, acts on your turn, and its numbers scale with the spell's level.", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 3rd."),
"Summon Undead": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (a gilded skull worth 300 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call an undead spirit: ghostly (flies through walls, frightens), putrid (poisons nearby, paralyzes) or skeletal (ranged grave bolts). It obeys you, acts on your turn, and its numbers scale with the spell's level.", "The spirit grows stronger for each level above 3rd."),
"Swift Quiver": ("1 bonus action", "Touch", "V, S, M (a quiver containing at least one piece of ammunition)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "Your quiver produces an endless supply of nonmagical ammunition. As a bonus action on each of your turns, you can make two attacks with a weapon that uses it.", ""),
"Blade Burst": ("1 action", "Self (5-foot radius)", "V", "Instantaneous",
  "Spectral blades sweep around you. Each creature within 5 feet makes a Dexterity save or takes 1d6 force damage. Damage grows to 2d6 at 5th level, 3d6 at 11th and 4d6 at 17th.", ""),
"Viper's Coil": None,
"Synaptic Static": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S", "Instantaneous",
  "A psychic burst erupts at a point. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere makes an Intelligence save, taking 8d6 psychic damage on a failure or half on a success. Those that fail are muddled for a minute: they subtract 1d6 from attacks, checks and concentration saves, repeating the save at the end of each turn.", ""),
"Bubbling Cauldron": ("1 action", "5 feet", "V, S, M (a gilded ladle worth 500 gp)", "10 minutes",
  "A claw-footed cauldron appears, filled with a potion of your choice of common or uncommon rarity that you've seen (DM approves). You can draw out a number of bottles equal to your spellcasting modifier; they vanish when you finish your next long rest if unused.", ""),
"Caustic Brew": ("1 action", "Self (30-foot line)", "V, S, M (a bit of rotten food)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A 30-foot line of acid sprays from you. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity save or is covered in acid, taking 2d4 acid damage at the start of each of its turns. A creature can use its action to scrape it off.", "Damage rises by 2d4 for each level above 1st."),
"Mind Whip": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V", "1 round",
  "You lash a creature's mind. It makes an Intelligence save. On a failure it takes 3d6 psychic damage, can't take reactions until its next turn ends, and on that turn can take only one of: move, action or bonus action. On a success it takes half damage only.", "One more creature for each level above 2nd."),
"Otherworldly Guise": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V, S, M (an object engraved with a symbol of the Outer Planes, worth 500 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You take on the aspect of the Lower or Upper Planes: immunity to fire and poison (lower) or radiant and necrotic (upper), immunity to being poisoned or charmed, spectral wings (flying 40 feet), +2 AC, magical weapon attacks, two attacks when you take the Attack action, and you can use your spellcasting ability for weapon attacks.", ""),
"Telepathy": ("1 action", "Unlimited", "V, S, M (a pair of linked silver rings)", "24 hours",
  "You create a telepathic link with a willing creature you know, on the same plane. You can share words, images, sounds and other sensory messages with each other for the duration.", ""),
"Temple of the Gods": ("1 hour", "120 feet", "V, S, M (a holy symbol worth at least 5 gp)", "24 hours",
  "A temple to your god rises from the ground: up to 120 feet on a side, 120 feet tall. Creatures of a type you name (or all who aren't your faith) have to pass a Charisma save to enter. Inside, divination and attempts to charm are hampered, and healing spells heal extra. Cast it in the same place every day for a year and it's permanent.", ""),
"Temporal Shunt": ("1 reaction, when a creature you see makes an attack or casts a spell", "120 feet", "V, S", "1 round",
  "You shunt a creature through time. It makes a Wisdom save or vanishes, and the attack or spell is wasted. It reappears at the start of its next turn, in the space it left (or nearest).", "One more creature for each level above 5th."),
"Mighty Transformation": ("1 action", "Self", "V, S, M (a few hairs from a bull)", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "You become a fighting machine: 50 temporary hit points, advantage on weapon attacks, an extra 2d12 force damage on weapon hits, proficiency with all armor, shields, simple and martial weapons, and Strength and Constitution saves, and two attacks when you take the Attack action. You can't cast spells. When it ends, you make a Constitution save or gain a level of exhaustion.", ""),
"Tether Essence": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a spool of platinum cord worth 250 gp, consumed)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "Two creatures you can see within 30 feet of each other make Constitution saves (with disadvantage if close). If both fail, they're tethered: damage one takes, the other takes too, and healing one heals the other. If one drops to 0 hit points, the other does too.", ""),
"Thorn Whip": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V, S, M (the stem of a plant with thorns)", "Instantaneous",
  "A long, thorny vine whips at a creature in range. Make a melee spell attack: 1d6 piercing damage, and a Large or smaller creature is pulled up to 10 feet toward you. Damage grows to 2d6 at 5th level, 3d6 at 11th and 4d6 at 17th.", ""),
"Thunder Step": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V", "Instantaneous",
  "You teleport to a space you can see within range, leaving a thunderclap behind. Each creature within 10 feet of where you left makes a Constitution save, taking 3d10 thunder damage on a failure or half on a success. You can bring one willing creature within 5 feet with you.", "Damage rises by 1d10 for each level above 3rd."),
"Thunderclap": ("1 action", "Self (5-foot radius)", "S", "Instantaneous",
  "A burst of thunder bangs out from you. Each creature other than you within 5 feet makes a Constitution save or takes 1d6 thunder damage. It can be heard 100 feet away. Damage grows to 2d6 at 5th level, 3d6 at 11th and 4d6 at 17th.", ""),
"Thunderous Smite": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "Your next melee weapon hit before the spell ends rings with thunder heard 300 feet away: an extra 2d6 thunder damage, and the target makes a Strength save or is pushed 10 feet and knocked prone.", ""),
"Tidal Wave": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S, M (a drop of water)", "Instantaneous",
  "A wave of water 30 feet long, 10 feet wide and 10 feet tall crashes down at a point. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity save, taking 4d8 bludgeoning damage and falling prone on a failure, or half and staying up on a success. The water spreads out and puts out fires.", ""),
"Time Ravage": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (an hourglass filled with diamond dust worth 5,000 gp, consumed)", "Instantaneous",
  "You age a creature you can see. It makes a Constitution save, taking 10d12 necrotic damage on a failure or half on a success. If it fails, it also ages to the brink of death: disadvantage on attacks, checks and saves, and its speed is halved. Only Wish or Greater Restoration cast with a 9th-level spell undoes it. Most creatures die of old age within 30 days.", ""),
"Tiny Helper": ("1 minute", "Touch", "V, S", "8 hours",
  "You bring a Tiny nonmagical object to life: it sprouts little arms and legs and becomes a creature that obeys you. It can carry small loads, scout, fetch things and fight weakly.", "Two more objects for each level above 3rd."),
"Toll the Dead": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S", "Instantaneous",
  "You point at a creature and the sound of a dolorous bell fills the air. It makes a Wisdom save or takes 1d8 necrotic damage, or 1d12 if it's already missing any hit points. Damage grows at 5th, 11th and 17th level.", ""),
"Transfix": None,
"Transmute Rock": ("1 action", "120 feet", "S, M (clay and water)", "Until dispelled",
  "Choose an area of stone or mud up to a 40-foot cube. Turn rock to mud (difficult terrain, creatures can sink and be restrained, and things above may fall) or mud to rock (creatures in it make a Dexterity save or are trapped in stone and restrained until they break free).", ""),
"Uncertain Footing": None,
"Vision of Elapsing Eons": None,
"Vortex Warp": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S", "Instantaneous",
  "You twist space around a creature you can see. It makes a Constitution save (or chooses to fail) or teleports to an unoccupied space you can see within range.", "The teleport range grows by 30 feet for each level above 2nd."),
"Wail of the Banshee": None,
"Wall of Light": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S, M (a hand mirror)", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "A shimmering wall of light, up to 60 feet long, 10 feet high and 5 feet thick, appears. It blocks sight, sheds bright light, and creatures in it when it appears make a Constitution save, taking 4d8 radiant damage and being blinded for a minute on a failure, or half damage only on a success. As an action you can fire a beam from it at a creature within 60 feet (a ranged spell attack, 4d8 radiant), shrinking the wall by 10 feet.", "Damage rises by 1d8 for each level above 5th."),
"Wall of Sand": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (a handful of sand)", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "A wall of swirling sand, up to 30 feet long, 10 feet high and 10 feet thick, appears. It blocks sight, and a creature moving through it is blinded inside and moves at a third of its speed.", ""),
"Wall of Water": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a drop of water)", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "A wall of water, up to 30 feet long, 10 feet high and 1 foot thick (or a ring 20 feet across), appears. It's difficult terrain, ranged weapon attacks through it have disadvantage, fire damage through it is halved, and cold damage can freeze sections solid.", ""),
"Wardaway": None,
"Warding Wind": ("1 action", "Self", "V", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "A strong wind (20 mph) blows around you in a 10-foot radius. It deafens you and others in it, puts out small flames, hedges out vapor and gas, makes the area difficult terrain for others, and gives ranged weapon attacks into or out of it disadvantage.", ""),
"Warp Sense": None,
"Watery Sphere": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V, S, M (a droplet of water)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A 5-foot-radius sphere of water forms. Up to four Medium or smaller creatures in it make a Strength save or are restrained inside. As an action you can move the sphere 30 feet; restrained creatures move with it. A creature can try to escape at the end of each of its turns.", ""),
"Waves of Exhaustion": None,
"Whirlwind": ("1 action", "300 feet", "V, M (a piece of straw)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A whirlwind 10 feet across and 30 feet tall howls down at a point. Each creature it touches makes a Dexterity save, taking 10d6 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. A Large or smaller creature that fails is pulled in and restrained, then flung out later. You can move it 30 feet as an action.", ""),
"Witch Bolt": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V, S, M (a twig from a tree struck by lightning)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A crackling beam of blue energy lances at a creature. Make a ranged spell attack: 1d12 lightning damage on a hit. On each of your turns you can use your action to deal 1d12 lightning to it automatically. The spell ends if it gets out of range or behind total cover.", "The first hit deals 1d12 more for each level above 1st."),
"Wither and Bloom": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a withered vine twisted into a loop)", "Instantaneous",
  "You call the decay and growth of nature at a point. Each creature you choose in a 10-foot-radius sphere makes a Constitution save, taking 2d6 necrotic damage on a failure or half on a success. Nonmagical plants there wither. Then one creature of your choice in the area can spend and roll one of its Hit Dice and heal that much plus your spellcasting modifier.", "Damage rises by 1d6, and the healed creature can spend one more Hit Die, for each level above 2nd."),
"Word of Radiance": ("1 action", "5 feet", "V, M (a holy symbol)", "Instantaneous",
  "You speak a divine word and burning light erupts. Each creature of your choice within 5 feet makes a Constitution save or takes 1d6 radiant damage. Damage grows to 2d6 at 5th level, 3d6 at 11th and 4d6 at 17th.", ""),
"Wrath of Nature": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You call the spirits of nature against your foes in a 60-foot cube. Trees lash enemies (Dexterity save or 4d6 slashing), grass and undergrowth become difficult terrain for them, roots and vines restrain (Strength save), and as a bonus action rocks fly at a creature for 3d8 bludgeoning and can knock it prone.", ""),
"Wrathful Smite": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "Your next melee weapon hit before the spell ends deals an extra 1d6 psychic damage, and the target makes a Wisdom save or is frightened of you until the spell ends. As an action it can make a Wisdom check against your DC to steel itself and end the spell.", ""),
"Wristpocket": ("1 action (ritual)", "Self", "S", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You send an object you're holding (5 pounds or less) to a pocket dimension. As a bonus action you can bring it back to your hand, or send it away again. When the spell ends, the object returns to your hand.", ""),
"Regal Presence": ("1 action", "Self (10-foot emanation)", "V, S, M (a miniature tiara)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You surround yourself with unearthly majesty. Each creature of your choice in the emanation when you cast it, or that enters it or ends its turn there, makes a Wisdom save, taking 4d6 psychic damage and being knocked prone or pushed 10 feet away on a failure, or half damage only on a success. A creature makes this save only once per turn.", ""),
"Zephyr Strike": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You move like the wind. Your movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks. Once before the spell ends, you can give yourself advantage on one weapon attack; if it hits, it deals an extra 1d8 force damage, and your speed rises by 30 feet until the end of that turn.", ""),
"Zone of Amicability": None,
}
